Subject: [PATCH] Use caller-selected ELF comparison tools

The SONiC Bazel equivalence checker owns the readelf and abidiff tool selection.
Pass those declared paths to compareELF instead of letting the CLI select host
tools. This preserves comparison policy while supporting sealed tool closures.

This downstream integration patch was carried by sonic-buildimage's checker at
54eb0632ba9dc93e784665280ce4ec19c122cef1 for compareELF 5f79c620. It is retained
for that pinned source; no upstream acceptance is claimed. Remove it when the
selected compareELF CLI supports equivalent explicit tool selection.

--- a/elfcompare.py
+++ b/elfcompare.py
@@ -434,6 +434,9 @@
     parser = build_parser()
     args = parser.parse_args(argv)
-    policy = ComparisonPolicy()
+    policy = ComparisonPolicy(
+        readelf=os.environ.get("ELFCOMPARE_READELF") or None,
+        abidiff=os.environ.get("ELFCOMPARE_ABIDIFF") or None,
+    )
-
+
     try:
         from elfcompare_tools import dump_json
